## Git workflow

- Default branch: `main`. Keep it shippable; do day-to-day work on feature branches.
- Branch naming: `feature/<short-name>`, `fix/<short-name>`, `docs/<short-name>`, `chore/<short-name>`.
- Before committing: run lint/format as required by the project; review `git diff`.
- Never commit secrets, `.env*`, credentials, or generated artifacts covered by `.gitignore`.
- Prefer small, logical commits; split unrelated changes.

## Commit messages (Conventional Commits)

- Format: `type(optional-scope): imperative summary` (English).
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `style`.
- Summary: imperative mood, ~50 chars, no trailing period; body optional for context.
- Align commits with layers and features: `docs/mhp/features/*/feature.md` updates can sit with implementation or as a dedicated `docs` commit.

## Pull requests

- Use clear titles and complete sentences in the description: what changed, why, how to verify.
- Link issues or tasks if the team uses them.